WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
What if moving through space didn't require physical
thrust, but just re-tuning a frequency?

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.500
The locational variable hypothesis suggests that
spatial

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.000
coordinates are actually an embedded internal
vibration.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
To test this, imagine a thin hollow copper sphere
resting on a pristine isolation table.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.946
This is SPHERE,

6
00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:27.000
a decentralized community-funded science collective
building a public metrology lab to find out.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.664
We start by recording the sphere's baseline acoustic
and electromagnetic resonance at position A,

8
00:00:32.664 --> 00:00:35.000
using a highly sensitive scanning laser.

9
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Then, we move the sphere to the exact opposite end
of the table and measure it again.

10
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.793
But to prevent fake results, the setup must be
flawlessly isolated from all thermal,

11
00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:48.000
seismic, and radio interference.

12
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
If our instruments detect a reproducible frequency
shift above 230 kHz between the two spots,

13
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.467
it indicates that physical location is an intrinsic,

14
00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:01.000
measurable property encoded inside the matter
itself.

15
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Join the public effort at the SPHERE Spatial
Positioning Harmonic Energy Resonance Experiment
website.

16
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
We need RF engineers, reviewers, and crowd funders.

17
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.000
So if this rigorous protocol actually succeeds, what
happens to that simple hollow copper sphere?

18
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Its shifted resonance wouldn't just be an anomalous
data point.

19
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
It would prove that location itself is an internal
vibration.
